# plumbline-reranker-v1

A cross-encoder reranker fine-tuned on hard negatives for **Plumbline**, a benchmark that races six retrieval pipelines against each other on an LLM-screened, human-adjudicated gold set and publishes retrieval quality, groundedness, latency and cost for each.

This checkpoint is **lane 6** of that benchmark. Lane 4 is the same pipeline with the stock `$base_model`. The checkpoint is the only difference between them — same `retrieve_depth=50`, same `rerank_depth=20`, same RRF `k=60`, same MRR@10 cutoff, same tie-breaks — which is what makes the delta attributable to the model rather than to the pipeline.

## Base model

[`$base_model`](https://huggingface.co/$base_model) — 22M parameters, `num_labels=1`. The existing MS MARCO relevance head is fine-tuned rather than replaced, so this starts from what that training left behind instead of from a random projection.

Saved with `save_pretrained` and no sentence-transformers configuration files, deliberately: the stock checkpoint is a plain HF sequence-classification repo, and an extra `config_sentence_transformers.json` here could set a different inference activation. Then the lane 4 → lane 6 delta would be partly a scoring convention rather than the weights.

